WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
Rosa considers moving value from a personally owned nonqualified annuity into

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.660
a different annuity. Section ten thirty-five can allow a qualifying exchange

3
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.800
without recognizing the existing gain at the time of the exchange.

4
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.960
It does not mean every transfer is eligible, every future payment

5
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.380
is excluded or every cost disappears.

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.180
The original contract category, the new contract category, the insured or

7
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.220
ownership interests and the actual transaction method matter.

8
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.160
A tax-favored exchange also is different from a retirement-account rollover.

9
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.920
Start with which contracts are involved and how the insurers will

10
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.580
carry out the exchange before promising a tax result.

11
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:43.060
Within the core life and annuity categories, a life insurance contract

12
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.520
can be exchanged for another life contract, an endowment or an

13
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.660
annuity when the other requirements are met.

14
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.160
An endowment can go to an eligible endowment or annuity.

15
00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.460
An annuity can go to another annuity.

16
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.100
The reverse move from an annuity to life insurance does not

17
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.580
qualify under this section.

18
00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.840
Neither does an annuity-to-endowment exchange.

19
00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:12.520
An endowment-to-endowment exchange has an additional requirement: the new

20
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.860
regular payments must begin no later than they would under the

21
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:21.300
old contract. The statute includes specified qualified long-term-care

22
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:26.480
directions as well; that is a separate contract category, not

23
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.060
permission to exchange any insurance product for any other.

24
00:01:30.786 --> 00:01:34.386
Marcus asks whether he can use an exchange to replace insurance

25
00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:38.266
on his own life with insurance on a different person.

26
00:01:39.226 --> 00:01:43.066
The exchange rules require the relevant insured identity to remain

27
00:01:43.066 --> 00:01:47.806
consistent; a different insured is not simply the same investment in

28
00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:53.266
a new wrapper. For annuity exchanges, the regulation also requires

29
00:01:53.266 --> 00:01:57.946
the same person or persons to remain entitled under the contracts

30
00:01:57.946 --> 00:02:03.046
as the obligees. Do not casually add or remove

31
00:02:03.046 --> 00:02:07.206
an owner while assuming tax treatment remains unchanged.

32
00:02:08.266 --> 00:02:12.506
The insurer must review the actual registration and contract facts.

33
00:02:13.606 --> 00:02:18.706
A new product name, an attractive illustration or the same premium

34
00:02:18.706 --> 00:02:22.586
amount does not substitute for meeting the identity requirements.

35
00:02:23.681 --> 00:02:27.061
Rosa asks the old insurer to send her the surrender money

36
00:02:27.061 --> 00:02:29.521
so she can buy the new annuity herself.

37
00:02:30.321 --> 00:02:33.181
That is not the same as an actual direct exchange or

38
00:02:33.181 --> 00:02:35.261
assignment processed between the insurers.

39
00:02:36.261 --> 00:02:39.601
An IRS ruling addressed a check issued to the owner and

40
00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:43.781
then endorsed to the second insurer: that endorsement did not turn

41
00:02:43.781 --> 00:02:45.701
the payment into a qualifying exchange.

42
00:02:46.721 --> 00:02:51.521
The nonqualified annuity payment remained taxable to the extent required by

43
00:02:51.521 --> 00:02:56.501
its distribution rules. Do not promise the sixty-day retirement rollover rule

44
00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.541
for this personal contract.

45
00:02:59.181 --> 00:03:02.541
Arrange the proper exchange process before the owner takes a distribution,

46
00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:07.401
and confirm that both insurers will handle the transaction as intended.

47
00:03:08.535 --> 00:03:13.182
Assume Rosa exchanges an annuity worth eighty thousand dollars with fifty

48
00:03:13.182 --> 00:03:17.095
thousand dollars of adjusted investment for a new annuity of equal

49
00:03:17.095 --> 00:03:21.995
value. The question states that all exchange requirements are met, with

50
00:03:21.995 --> 00:03:25.755
no cash received, debt, charges or other adjustment.

51
00:03:26.595 --> 00:03:30.195
The thirty thousand dollars of gain is not recognized currently, and

52
00:03:30.195 --> 00:03:33.495
the fifty thousand dollar basis carries into the replacement under these

53
00:03:33.495 --> 00:03:38.675
facts. It does not become eighty thousand dollars of fresh after-tax

54
00:03:38.675 --> 00:03:44.055
investment. Receiving cash or discharging policy debt can introduce taxable

55
00:03:44.055 --> 00:03:46.095
gain under additional rules.

56
00:03:47.115 --> 00:03:51.875
A life policy received in exchange for a modified endowment contract

57
00:03:51.875 --> 00:03:55.335
also retains that classification under the applicable rule.

58
00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:58.615
Check these features before using the simple example.

59
00:03:59.452 --> 00:04:03.492
A qualifying exchange can still involve surrender charges, new restrictions,

60
00:04:04.132 --> 00:04:08.192
lost benefits, different guarantees or higher ongoing expenses.

61
00:04:08.912 --> 00:04:12.292
Rosa should compare the entire transaction with keeping the existing

62
00:04:12.292 --> 00:04:17.272
contract. For a covered Maryland annuity recommendation, the best-interest

63
00:04:17.272 --> 00:04:22.052
and replacement review includes the actual costs, benefits and required

64
00:04:22.052 --> 00:04:27.372
consumer information. A producer should not describe tax nonrecognition as

65
00:04:27.372 --> 00:04:28.972
proof that the replacement is better.

66
00:04:28.972 --> 00:04:33.892
Partial annuity exchanges have additional rules, including a timing test for

67
00:04:33.892 --> 00:04:37.712
later distributions, so they should not be treated as automatically identical

68
00:04:37.712 --> 00:04:39.172
to a complete exchange.

69
00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:44.672
On an exam, identify the allowed direction, correct method and carryover

70
00:04:44.672 --> 00:04:48.732
result, then keep the separate contract
and recommendation consequences in view.
